      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> War sustains at current kinetic pace, with daily exchanges and Hormuz at 10-15% of normal traffic, through the Israeli election cycle (<span class="cite">F5</span>) — neither side has the domestic-political tolerance for a third failed framework before November.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> A third bilateral framework materializes by November 30 (<span class="cite">F9</span> at 20%) if Pezeshkian's standing MOU offer finds a US counterpart and Oman brokers a named halt before Washington's post-election political calendar constrains flexibility.</p>
